Title:
MicroSocks11 – A cross-platform SOCKS5 server (and library)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- MicroSocks11 is a C++11/CMake-based reimplementation/port of the original `microsocks` project, providing a lightweight SOCKS5 proxy server plus a reusable static library (`socks5`).  
- It solves the need for a small, portable SOCKS5 server that can be built across platforms (including Windows via MSVC/vcpkg) and optionally shipped as a mostly-standalone static binary.  
- The project supports IPv4, IPv6, and DNS (including SOCKS5 hostname resolution use cases), and exposes CLI options for bind/listen configuration, verbosity, and username/password authentication.  
- It includes an “auth-once” mode that whitelists an IP after successful authentication to avoid repeated credential prompts on subsequent connections.  
- Useful for red teams/pentesters needing quick pivoting infrastructure, and for developers who want to embed SOCKS5 proxy capability into other tooling via the provided library API.  
- Notable operationally: it ships with Docker support and documents static build caveats on Linux (glibc `getaddrinfo` static linking issues; recommends clang/libc++).

Technical Focus:
- SOCKS5 protocol implementation (proxy server + library)
- Cross-platform C++ build tooling (CMake, MSVC, vcpkg)
- IPv4/IPv6 networking and DNS/hostname handling
- Optional static linking and portability constraints (glibc vs libc++)
- Containerized deployment (Docker, host networking)

Use Cases:
- Stand up a lightweight SOCKS5 pivot point on an internal host or jump box
- Provide a local proxy endpoint for tooling that supports SOCKS5 (curl, scanners, custom agents)
- Embed SOCKS5 server functionality into custom red team utilities via the `socks5` static library
- Run a disposable proxy service in Docker for lab/testing or ephemeral infrastructure
- Test client behavior against SOCKS5 auth and DNS/hostname proxying

Keywords:
SOCKS5, proxy server, C++11, CMake, static library, IPv4, IPv6, DNS, getaddrinfo, authentication, username/password, IP whitelisting, BUILD_STATIC, MSVC, vcpkg, cxxopts, Docker, --net=host, curl --socks5-hostname, microsocks